IIUC the pattern goes like this:

```js
const openedFromCli = inspector.url() !== undefined;
if (!openedFromCli) {
  inspector.open(0, undefined, false); // first call to set the inspector.url()
}
inspector.open(openedFromCli ? undefined : 0, undefined, true);
```

Does changing the last call of `inspector.open()` to `inspector.waitForDebugger()` works? Previously, calling it the second time with `inspector.open(undefined, undefined, true)` roughly did the same thing as `inspector.waitForDebugger()` other than that it resets the port integer and the host string stored on the native side without actually doing anything about them (and that was why the url returned again showed these modified values).
